# A display plugged in or pulled out while the desktop is running.
#
# The kernel emits a `change` uevent on the drm subsystem when a connector's
# state alters -- which is exactly what plugging an HDMI cable into a
# television does. Without this rule nothing reacted: the session configured
# the outputs once at start-up and never looked again, so a TV connected after
# boot stayed dark no matter what.
#
# The helper needs an X display and the session's authority to talk to the
# server, so it is run through a small wrapper that finds them.
ACTION=="change", SUBSYSTEM=="drm", ENV{HOTPLUG}=="1", RUN+="/opt/notebook/display-hotplug.sh"
